<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Mainland Southeast Asia</p><h1 class="st-title">Mac dynasty</h1><p class="st-meta">1527 CE – 1592 CE · capital Thang Long</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Vietnamese dynasty founded by the general Mac Dang Dung, who usurped the Le throne in 1527 and fought a long civil war against Le loyalists.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mac-dang-dung">Mac Dang Dung</a>, a fisherman's son who rose to command the Le court guard, took advantage of the weak late <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/later-le-dynasty">Later Le dynasty</a> and in 1527 forced the emperor to abdicate, founding his own dynasty at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thang-long">Thang Long</a>. In 1540 he avoided a threatened Ming invasion by ceding border districts and accepting the lower rank of commissioner.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The Mac kept Le institutions, holding examinations regularly and promoting trade and crafts in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-river-asia">Red River</a> delta. Their opponents, led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nguyen-kim">Nguyen Kim</a> and then <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trinh-kiem">Trinh Kiem</a>, restored a Le emperor in 1533 in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thanh-hoa">Thanh Hoa</a>, beginning the war between the Northern Mac and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/revival-le-dynasty">Southern Le</a> courts.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The war lasted until 1592, when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trinh-tung">Trinh Tung</a> captured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thang-long">Thang Long</a> and executed the Mac emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mac-mau-hop">Mac Mau Hop</a>. Mac survivors, with Ming protection, kept a rump state in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cao-bang">Cao Bang</a> until 1677, known as the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/mac-rule-in-cao-bang">Mac rule in Cao Bang</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/mac-dynasty.jpg" alt="Mac dynasty" width="320" height="394"><figcaption>Image: TRMC · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Map_of_Southern_and_Northern_Dynasties_of_Vietnam.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1527 CE – 1592 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Thang Long</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Mac Dang Dung, Mac Mau Hop</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Confucianism, Buddhism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Vietnamese, Classical Chinese</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/vietnam">Vietnam</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Nhà Mạc</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1560&amp;focus=mac-dynasty" aria-label="Mac dynasty on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="7610 1566 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Mac dynasty lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M7930 1822L7643 1242M7930 1822L7930 1822M7930 1822L7843 1596"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7643 1242h0M7930 1822h0M7843 1596h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7930 1822h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7930 1822h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1560&amp;focus=mac-dynasty">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
